+# Spec: EPMCDME-12616 — Enhance Workflow Edit with Refine/Modify with AI and Revert to Previous
+
+## Summary
+
+Add two new actions to the Workflow Edit page:
+
+1. **Refine with AI** — a feature-flagged button that opens a two-step flow (optional prompt popup → AI modal) and injects the AI-generated YAML back into both editor modes. User must still click Save to persist.
+2. **Revert to Previous** — a feature-flagged button that calls `POST /v1/workflows/{id}/revert`, which auto-saves the revert server-side and returns the updated workflow. The frontend resets the form from the response — no separate Save needed.
+
+Action history logging is server-side only (`yaml_config_history` tracks every save/revert). No frontend audit-log UI is required.
+
+---
+
+## API Contracts (confirmed with backend)
+
+### `POST /v1/workflows/{workflow_id}/refine`
+
+**Request body:**
+```json
+{
+  "yaml_config": "<current yaml>",
+  "refine_prompt": "<optional instruction>",
+  "llm_model": "gpt-4o",
+  "project": "my-project"
+}
+```
+(`llm_model` and `project` are optional; frontend always omits them — backend uses defaults.)
+
+**Response:**
+```json
+{ "yaml_config": "<complete revised yaml>" }
+```
+
+**Error envelope:**
+```json
+{ "error": { "message": "...", "details": "...", "help": "..." } }
+```
+Read `error.message` for the user-facing string. `details` and `help` are optional.
+
+| Status | Cause |
+|---|---|
+| `400` | LLM returned invalid/unparseable YAML |
+| `403` | User lacks WRITE permission |
+| `404` | Workflow not found |
+| `429` | LLM quota / rate limit exceeded |
+| `500` | Unexpected AI chain error |
+
+**Latency:** 5–20 seconds. Show spinner from request start; show "this is taking longer than expected" at 15 s; hard client-side timeout at 60 s.
+
+---
+
+### `POST /v1/workflows/{workflow_id}/revert`
+
+**Request body:** none
+
+**Response envelope** (same as `PUT /v1/workflows/{id}`):
+```json
+{ "message": "...", "data": <Workflow> }
+```
+Frontend reads `data` to refresh the editor without a follow-up GET.
+
+**Error envelope:** same shape as refine — read `error.message`.
+
+---
+
+## Feature Flag
+
+- Constant: `WORKFLOW_AI_REFINE_FLAG = 'workflowAIRefine'` in `src/constants/workflows.ts`
+- Checked in `EditWorkflowPage` via `useFeatureFlag(WORKFLOW_AI_REFINE_FLAG)`
+- **Defaults to enabled** when the config item is absent from `v1/config`
+- When flag is off, neither button renders
+
+---
+
+## Architecture
+
+```
+EditWorkflowPage
+  ├── "Refine with AI" button        (feature-flagged)
+  ├── "Revert to Previous" button    (feature-flagged, disabled when history empty)
+  ├── RefineWorkflowPromptPopup      (step 1: optional prompt)
+  ├── RefineWorkflowModal            (step 2: show AI result, apply to editor)
+  ├── ConfirmationModal              (revert confirmation)
+  └── WorkflowForm key={formKey}
+        ├── Refine path: formRef.replaceYamlConfig(yaml) → editor update + blockTransition()
+        └── Revert path: workflowsStore.revertWorkflow(id) → update currentWorkflow → increment formKey → form remounts clean
+```
+
+**Refine flow:**
+1. Click "Refine with AI" → `showPromptPopup = true`
+2. Submit optional prompt → `showRefineModal = true`, modal calls `workflowsStore.refineWorkflowWithAI`
+3. On success → user clicks "Apply Changes" → `formRef.current.replaceYamlConfig(yaml_config)` → editor updates, guard re-armed
+4. Toast: "AI refine applied — save to confirm"
+
+**Revert flow:**
+1. Click "Revert to Previous" → `showRevertConfirm = true`
+2. User confirms → `workflowsStore.revertWorkflow(id)` → backend auto-saves
+3. Update `workflowsStore.currentWorkflow` with `response.data`
+4. Increment `formKey` → `WorkflowForm` remounts with the reverted workflow as initial state (clean baseline, no unsaved-changes warning)
+5. Toast: "Reverted to previous version"
+
+---
+
+## New Types (`src/types/entity/workflow.ts`)
+
+```ts
+export interface WorkflowAIRefineFields {
+  yaml_config: string
+  refine_prompt?: string
+}
+
+export interface WorkflowAIRefineResponse {
+  yaml_config: string
+}
+
+export interface WorkflowRevertResponse {
+  message: string
+  data: Workflow
+}
+```
+
+---
+
+## Store (`src/store/workflows.ts`)
+
+Two new methods on both the `WorkflowsStore` interface and `workflowsStore` proxy:
+
+```ts
+refineWorkflowWithAI(id: string, fields: WorkflowAIRefineFields): Promise<WorkflowAIRefineResponse> {
+  return api.post(`v1/workflows/${id}/refine`, fields).then((r) => r.json())
+},
+
+revertWorkflow(id: string): Promise<WorkflowRevertResponse> {
+  return api.post(`v1/workflows/${id}/revert`).then((r) => r.json())
+},
+```
+
+---
+
+## New Components
+
+### `RefineWorkflowPromptPopup`
+
+**Path:** `src/pages/workflows/components/RefineWorkflowPromptPopup.tsx`
+
+Mirrors `RefineWithAIPromptPopup` from the assistants module.
+
+- Props: `isVisible: boolean`, `onHide: () => void`, `onRefine: (prompt: string) => void`
+- Header: "Refine Workflow with AI"
+- Body: description text + optional `<Textarea>` (React Hook Form + Yup, field `refine_prompt?: string`)
+- Footer: Cancel (SECONDARY) + "Refine with AI" (MAGICAL)
+- `dismissableMask={false}`, auto-focus textarea on open
+
+### `RefineWorkflowModal`
+
+**Path:** `src/pages/workflows/components/RefineWorkflowModal.tsx`
+
+- Props: `visible: boolean`, `workflowId: string`, `refineFields: WorkflowAIRefineFields`, `onHide: () => void`, `onApply: (yaml: string) => void`
+- On mount: calls `workflowsStore.refineWorkflowWithAI(workflowId, refineFields)`; shows 15 s timeout warning via `setTimeout`; cancels request on unmount if possible
+- On hide: resets response/error/timeout state
+- States:
+  - **Loading** — spinner + "Analyzing your Workflow configuration" + warning after 15 s: "This is taking longer than expected…"
+  - **Response** — read-only YAML preview in `<AceEditor>` (readonly mode, same editor used elsewhere in the workflow UI)
+  - **Error** — `error.message` from response + "Try Again" button
+- Footer (response state only): "Close" (SECONDARY) + "Apply Changes" (PRIMARY)
+- `className="max-w-4xl w-full"`, `overlayClassName="z-60"`, `bodyClassName="max-h-[calc(90vh-200px)] overflow-y-auto"`
+
