+
+## WorkflowFormRef Changes (refine path only)
+
+New method for AI refine YAML injection:
+
+```ts
+replaceYamlConfig: (yaml: string) => void
+```
+
+- **Visual editor path:** calls `editorRef.current.setYamlConfig(yaml)` then `blockTransition()`; also updates local `yamlConfig` state
+- **Legacy form path:** calls `formFieldsRef.current.setYamlConfig(yaml)` then `blockTransition()`; also updates local `yamlConfig` state
+
+The revert path does **not** use `replaceYamlConfig` — it remounts `WorkflowForm` via `formKey`.
+
+---
+
+## WorkflowEditorRef Changes
+
+```ts
+setYamlConfig: (yaml: string) => void
+```
+
+Deserializes YAML using the existing `deserialize()` utility, then replaces nodes/edges on the ReactFlow canvas via the same mechanism used by the YAML panel's restore action.
+
+---
+
+## WorkflowFormFieldsRef Changes
+
+```ts
+setYamlConfig: (yaml: string) => void
+```
+
+Calls React Hook Form `setValue('yaml_config', yaml, { shouldDirty: true })`.
+
+---
+
+## UnsavedChanges Guard
+
+- **Refine path:** `replaceYamlConfig` calls `blockTransition()` after updating the YAML — re-arms the guard so the user is warned if navigating away before saving.
+- **Revert path:** `formKey` increment remounts `WorkflowForm` fresh from the already-saved `currentWorkflow`. The baseline and current state are identical, so no unsaved-changes warning fires.
+
